# DBVO Dialogue Tweaks — the player-voice BOOST (slider above 100%), verified in-engine.
#
# What it proves, hands-free: with the slider at 250%, the DLL's SetVolumeImpl hook fires on the
# player's own DBVO line, on the audio thread, finds that sound in the audio manager's map, and
# XAudio2 accepts a gain above 1.0 — the engine's own volume path clamps at 1.0, which is why the
# slider used to stop at 100. The evidence is the DLL's readback line in its log:
#     voice boost x2.50: voice V -> V*2.5 (sound N)
# and the last step asserts on exactly that substring (the multiplier, not the readback: the
# readback depends on the profile's master volume).
#
#   mods/DBVODialogueTweaks/stage-test-profile.sh          # build both stages (once, after ./package.sh)
#   SKYTEST_NO_AUTOLOAD=1 skytest replay ~/.cache/skytest-dbvotweaks \
#       mods/DBVODialogueTweaks/voiceboost.steps --headless --no-shots      # must PASS
#
# The A/B for the hook itself — the SAME stage with the DLL deleted, nothing else changed:
#   SKYTEST_NO_AUTOLOAD=1 skytest replay ~/.cache/skytest-dbvotweaks-nodll \
#       mods/DBVODialogueTweaks/voiceboost.steps --headless --no-shots      # must FAIL at the log gate
# And the control for the slider semantics is voiceboost-control.steps (same stage, 100%, no line).
#
# Only the console is driven: the boost needs a player line, not a conversation, so no NPC is
# placed and no topic is clicked — every extra step would be flake surface that exercises nothing.
# The slider value reaches the DLL through the same Papyrus native the MCM uses, dispatched by
# SkytestProbe's `papyrus-call` (the direct-call form of a Papyrus global), so the stage needs
# no SkyUI (none is staged — see stage-test-profile.sh). Not the console: on 1.7.104 neither
# `cgf` nor `callglobalfunction` exists ("Script command … not found", verified 2026-09-08).
# The ack only means "queued on the VM", hence the 1 s settle before the line is spoken. Path
# arguments to the console MUST be quoted (it splits an unquoted one at `/`).
#
# NO_AUTOLOAD because the bundled po3_StartOnSave is stale for 1.7.104, so boot-into-save is
# unavailable and the script drives the main menu itself. Drop that env var once Start On Save
# 2.8.0 lands in skytest/base-skse/ AND delete the first five steps.
#
# Pixel coordinates are for the headless default 1280x720; re-read them off a `shot` if the
# session resolution changes.

# --- boot: main menu -> the SkytestBase save (QASmoke) ------------------------------
click 1177 496          # CONTINUE — a coordinate click; a bare `enter` here is unreliable (#25)
wait 2s
tap enter               # "Continue from your last saved game?" -> Yes
wait 4s
click 602 409           # "Creations are currently loaded … continue?" -> Yes (#25). Harmless if absent.
wait until:inworld
wait 3s                 # inworld fires before the player's 3D settles (#16)

# --- set the slider to 250% through the DLL's Papyrus native --------------------------
cmd {"cmd":"papyrus-call","class":"DBVOTweaks","function":"SetPlayerVoiceVolume","args":[2.5]}
wait 1s

# --- speak the player's line (the ConsoleUtil substitute) ---------------------------
tap tilde
wait until:menu:Console
type player.speaksound "dbvo/t1.fuz"
tap enter
# A timing witness, not a query: this line's `t` in trace.jsonl marks when the audio started.
cmd {"cmd":"status"}
tap tilde
wait until:!menu:Console

# --- THE ASSERTION --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The DLL logged the boosted readback for this line. Without the DLL (nodll stage) or with the
# slider at 100% (control script) this line never appears and the gate times out.
wait until:log:DBVODialogueTweaks|voice boost x2.50
